mended for  immunocompromised people  we are going to be offering a spring  booster for elders and seniors in  british columbia as the people being  most at risk  bc is already set to roll out second  boosters for people 70 and older  indigenous people over the age of 55 and  those who are immunocompromised only  about half of the people in that  province have received their first  booster shot  and masks remain one of the most  effective ways to prevent virus  transmission many provinces though have  already lifted their mask mandates two  are now extending those mandates quebec  is extending its mass mandate for indoor  public spaces until the end of the month  as that province deals with an uptick in  new infections and hospitalizations and  masks will still be worn in pei until  april 28th though the provincial state  of emergency there will end at midnight  and capacity limits will be lifted  like oil and water ahead how canada's  climate goals clash with new global  energy demands  you're watching global national  [Music]  this week's report from the u.n  intergovernmental panel on climate  change was clear the world is running  out of time and options at the same time  russia's invasion of ukraine has  countries looking for other sources of  oil and gas that's prompted the canadian  government to challenge the energy  sector here can you ramp up production  and scale back greenhouse gas emissions  as heather urex west explains it's put  the industry and its investors in a  delicate spot  the world needs oil and canada has it  but when it comes to energy things are  never so simple it's certainly a time of  a lot of turbulence obviously you have  these very short-term  impacts with the war in  ukraine the wall street journal is  reporting the white house wants more  canadian oil coming into the u.s but  only by rail or existing pipelines  keystone xl remains off the table  because while the world needs more  energy it also needs global emissions  cut and fast 